+\subsection{Byte Miss Ratio}
+Fig.~\ref{fig:bmr-box-6groups} reports BMR ratio distributions ($x/\mathrm{LRU}$).
+Compared with OMR, BMR is more sensitive to size skew; nevertheless, RSD remains in the leading tier in most groups.
+This behavior is consistent with the middle-layer design: size-sensitive terms and cross-feature interactions allow RSD to retain high value-density objects while still reacting to recency/frequency shifts.
+As a result, RSD achieves stable byte-level savings instead of sacrificing BMR for object-level gains.
