+\subsection{Robustness}
+We evaluate robustness from three views: rank consistency, percentile behavior, and dual-metric balance.
+
+\textbf{Rank-based robustness.}
+Fig.~\ref{fig:robust-rank} compares rank distributions under OMR and BMR ratio metrics ($x/\mathrm{LRU}$).
+RSD stays near the top ranks across groups, showing that its advantage is not tied to a specific trace family.
+The main reason is structural: the middle layer provides a stable inductive bias via representative features, while background learning updates only the weights to adapt to shifts.
+
